# tesseract-ocr 5.5.2-r0 (Alpine). No fixed release exists anywhere upstream
# as of 2026-09 (checked Alpine edge: still 5.5.3-r0, which the CVEs say is
# also affected) - these are not "upgrade available" findings.
# Both require Tesseract to load an attacker-crafted .traineddata model file
# to trigger (stack/heap overflow while parsing NORMPROTO / NT_SOFTMAX
# layers). This gateway only ever loads the single trusted eng.traineddata
# shipped by Alpine's tesseract-ocr-data-eng package - ocr.py/ocr_api.py
# never accept a user-supplied model path or let request input choose which
# .traineddata loads. Not reachable via the /v1/ocr endpoint.
CVE-2026-88047
CVE-2026-88048
